      "title": "Troubleshooting HTTP 504 and DNS Failures in Customer Portal",
      "content_summary": "Addresses HTTP 504 errors, DNS lookup failures, and certificate warnings in the Customer Portal, typically caused by network or firewall misconfigurations.",
      "content_body": "When users encounter HTTP 504 timeouts or DNS resolution errors in the Customer Portal, first verify that the corporate firewall allows traffic to the required Secret Store and Customer Portal endpoints. Check for any recent changes in network configuration that might block outbound DNS queries. Ensure that proxy settings are correctly defined, as a misconfigured proxy often causes certificate warnings alongside timeouts. Finally, update your firewall rules to permit the necessary IP ranges and DNS servers to resolve the connectivity issues."
